#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Run sqlfluff pytest nodes in place and trace their calls (the trace step
of the S7 trace oracle, docs/decisions/s7-tests-design.md, "Trace oracle").

Run it with the Python of a pinned oracle that scripts/setup installs. The
oracle script (scripts/s7-tests/oracle) starts it; run it alone only to
look at a trace:

  .tools/sqlfluff-oracle/bin/python scripts/s7-tests/trace-nodes \\
      --out out/s7-tests/trace.json NODE...
  .tools/sqlfluff-rs-oracle/bin/python scripts/s7-tests/trace-nodes --rust \\
      --out out/s7-tests/trace-rs.json NODE...

It runs the nodes with pytest in the sqlfluff root (or --root, for the unit
tests), as the sqlfluff tests run. With --rust, each FluffConfig gets the
Rust parser and rules (scripts/sqlfluff_oracle.py, force_rust), as the S1
oracles do. It records, for each node:

- outcome: the pytest outcome (passed, failed, skipped, or error). A failed
  setup or teardown is an error, also if the call passed.
- calls: each outermost call of the CLI (click.testing.CliRunner.invoke of
  a sqlfluff command), of the simple API (sqlfluff.lint, fix, parse), of a
  Linter path method (Linter.lint_path, lint_paths), and of a Linter string
  method (Linter.lint_string, lint_string_wrapped), and of a known test
  helper of sqlfluff.utils.testing.rules (HELPERS), in order, with its
  inputs and its outputs. A call inside a traced call is part of it. Only a
  Linter string call in a simple-API call with a config, and the Linter
  calls of a test helper, are recorded too, under "inner" of that call.
- error calls (kind "error"): a FluffConfig construction, a Linter
  construction, or a RuleSet.get_rulepack call outside each traced call that
  raises an exception (for example in pytest.raises). The call records the
  error and the CLI input of its config. If the trace can give the config
  to the CLI (a .sqlfluff file of the config model, or lint options), it
  runs "lint -" with that input and an empty stdin in a new folder, in
  process, and records the outputs and the errors of the same functions in
  that CLI run (the proof that the CLI gives the same error).
- untraced: each sqlfluff CLI command (click Command.main, get_config of
  the CLI) and each simple-API config (get_simple_config) that runs outside
  a traced call of its kind. Thus a call that the trace does not record is
  seen. untraced_linter (only if not empty): each Linter render or parse
  (Linter.render_string, parse_rendered) outside each traced call, for
  example Linter.parse_string.
- The temporary folders of the node (tempfile.mkdtemp, and the tmp_path
  and tmpdir fixtures). A CLI argument or working folder in one of them is
  {tmp}; the call records the files of the folder before and after it.
- The config of each Linter string call: the .sqlfluff text of the config
  model (s7config.py), and the keys that the CLI config from that file does
  not give (the proof; it must be empty). A Linter path call with a config
  that is not from FluffConfig.from_path records the overrides of the config
  and the keys that FluffConfig(overrides=...) does not give. A Linter made
  with dialect, rules, or exclude_rules (and no config) records the same
  model of its config ("kwargs_config" of the Linter inputs).
- processes: each program start, fork, and new Python process (the audit
  events and trace/sitecustomize.py, as scripts/s7-tests/config-readers).
  The trace does not record calls in another process.

Calls, untraced runs, and processes outside a node are under "outside".
The trace also records the sqlfluff config of the root folder (it must be
empty) and, with --rust, the parse runs of each parser.
"""

